From 9b2819bdc5a9a08713eb6fefcf8c239180f9f017 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dquillman <davequillman@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:45:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] a11y: fix every Lighthouse accessibility failure on the
 landing page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lighthouse accessibility 91 -> 100 on the homepage, verified by running
Lighthouse 13.4.1 against the built dist before and after. Four distinct
defects, 36 failing nodes.

1. Contrast — 36 nodes, all of them real

   text-slate-500 on the page grounds is 4.23:1 (slate-950), 3.85:1 (card)
   and 3.74:1 (slate-900). AA wants 4.5:1, and nearly every use of it here is
   10-12px mono, which is not "large text" under any reading of the rule.
   text-slate-600 is worse: 2.66:1 / 2.42:1. Both are lifted to slate-400
   (7.66:1 / 6.97:1 / 6.78:1), which is still clearly a muted tone.

   Two special cases the colour swap alone didn't fix:
   - The step pills in InteractiveDemo used slate-600 for "not reached yet".
     Now slate-400/80 — the active and visited states already carry that
     distinction, so no information is lost.
   - "Restarting demo..." carried animate-pulse. Pulse animates opacity toward
     zero, so axe samples the text mid-fade at 1.1:1 regardless of the colour
     token. Removed the pulse from the text.

2. Prohibited ARIA on the decode headline

   <span className="decode-word" aria-label={text}> — aria-label on a generic
   element with no role has nothing to name. Axe flags it, and screen readers
   may announce nothing, which means the headline word was simply missing for
   AT users while the scrambling glyphs beneath it were aria-hidden. The real
   word is now visually-hidden text; the animation stays hidden from AT.

3. No <main> landmark

   Landing.tsx was the only public page without one — Story, ExamLensGlossary
   and LandingShell all have it. Everything between </nav> and the footer is
   now wrapped in <main id="main">, so the skip-to-content path works here too.

4. Comparison table had no row headers

   The pricing comparison table's feature-name column was <td>, and the header
   cell above it was an empty <th />. Column headers now carry scope="col",
   the feature name is a <th scope="row">, and the empty corner cell gets an
   sr-only "Feature" label.

Not addressed here, deliberately: Lighthouse performance is 75 locally, and
the dominant cost is DecodeWord's REPLAY_MS = 12000 re-scrambling the H1
forever, which keeps the page visually unstable and pins Speed Index around
10.9s against a 2.2s LCP. That animation is a documented owner decision
(EC-030), so it stays until Dave calls it.

Verified: tsc -b clean, vite build clean, prerender 23/23, Lighthouse
accessibility 100 with zero remaining failures.

